<workout_file>
    <author>Coach Library</author>
    <name>Recovery Spin 30 min</name>
    <description>PICK THIS WHEN: The day after a race or a very hard session, or when the legs are flat.
DAY TYPE: Special.

Tests &amp; Openers. Recovery Spin 30 min.

Structure: 5 min warm-up, 20 min @ 50%, 5 min cool-down.

Coach notes: Thirty very easy minutes to flush the legs the day after a hard session or a race. If in doubt, take the day off instead.

Duration: 30 min. Estimated TSS: 12 (tests depend on your effort).</description>
    <sportType>bike</sportType>
    <tags>
        <tag name="Test"/>
    </tags>
    <workout>
        <Warmup Duration="300" PowerLow="0.40" PowerHigh="0.50">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="Recovery spin. The goal is to feel better at the end than at the start."/>
            <textevent timeoffset="180" message="2 minutes to the main set. Lift the effort slightly."/>
        </Warmup>
        <SteadyState Duration="1200" Power="0.50">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="20 min at 50%. Light gear, no pressure on the pedals."/>
            <textevent timeoffset="600" message="Halfway. If 50% feels like work today, lower the bias."/>
        </SteadyState>
        <Cooldown Duration="300" PowerLow="0.50" PowerHigh="0.40">
            <textevent timeoffset="0" message="Well done. Cool down easy."/>
        </Cooldown>
    </workout>
</workout_file>
